{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/950304-a-non-earth-world-of-darkness","id":950304,"title":"A non earth World of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-13T16:36:52-07:00","id":950304,"title":"A non earth World of Darkness","content":"Has any one made a ST a chronicle using cWoD titles in a game that was not set in a Earth setting? Like for example, purely a example mind you, use WtA in a Faerun setting? Or Mage in a space opera setting? I have been toying with the idea and just curious if anyone else has done this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T16:43:13-07:00","id":950308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/950304-a-non-earth-world-of-darkness#post950304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or Mage in a space opera setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>As we speak!<br /> <br /> (Well, not this exact second, but with my group for our current game.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T17:10:34-07:00","id":950320,"title":"","content":"So how have you set up the game? Did you let the Players use Traditions?: Or is the game a Technocracy game bout exploring the Deep Umbra? Or is it truly a space opera game where the Players visit different planets in the physical world?<br /> <br /> I am toying with the concept of Earth after the Time of Judgement happened and it was devastating. Society fell, civilization was practically destroyed. And the aftermath would have the Awakened Creatures controlling territories. I am thinking of mixing nWoD with cWoD. Vampires would use Requiem, Werewolves would use Garou, Mages would use Ascension, Changelings would use Lost. Thats as far as I have gotten with it so far though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T17:43:59-07:00","id":950333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/950304-a-non-earth-world-of-darkness?p=950320#post950320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how have you set up the game? Did you let the Players use Traditions?: Or is the game a Technocracy game bout exploring the Deep Umbra? Or is it truly a space opera game where the Players visit different planets in the physical world?<br /> <br /> I am toying with the concept of Earth after the Time of Judgement happened and it was devastating. Society fell, civilization was practically destroyed. And the aftermath would have the Awakened Creatures controlling territories. I am thinking of mixing nWoD with cWoD. Vampires would use Requiem, Werewolves would use Garou, Mages would use Ascension, Changelings would use Lost. Thats as far as I have gotten with it so far though</div> </div> </div> </div>We're actually using MtAw--sorry, I saw the thread on the far right under most recently created threads and didn't realize this was for CWoD--but the game is set in the 2800s, with different planets and three alien races.<br /> <br /> Feel free to ask more specifics, and I'll answer to the best of my ability. I just don't want to talk your ear off if I'm not sure what specifically would be helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T18:06:43-07:00","id":950343,"title":"","content":"Faerun would be difficult because of the assumptions about good and evil, order and chaos, arcane magic and divine magic, etc. If I was to do it, I would make my own world, to support the existence of the creatures. And I would through out the concept of Consensus because it is a piss poor idea, it always has been.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T18:15:09-07:00","id":950347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/950304-a-non-earth-world-of-darkness?p=950333#post950333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Feel free to ask more specifics, and I'll answer to the best of my ability. I just don't want to talk your ear off if I'm not sure what specifically would be helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm at least curious. So can all of the races be Mages? And are there any other surviving supernaturals?<br /> <br /> For the OP, I remember reading through a write-up years ago for a changeling game set in the future, with the different Kiths navigating space. Never got to play at all, but it was a really interesting setting.<br /> I've played in a Dark Ages game that was closer to high fantasy than realism. Not exactly another world, but close. There were bygones out in the wilderness and we dealt with at least 1 dragon attack on a town.<br /> There have also been a number of games I've ran where the PCs visited &quot;other realms&quot;. Technically somewhere in the Umbra, but entire worlds unto themselves (each only lasted about a story).<br /> <br /> And my wife was using the WoD system to set up a Dark Tower series game. I don't know how far she had gotten though or where those notes would be. Adult life got in the way of playing games as much as we would like.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T18:24:38-07:00","id":950352,"title":"","content":"Faerun was a example not what I was trying. I think a homebrew setting would be the way to go in my opinion too. I am just curious if any one has done this and what have they done. And I would like to know more bout the MtAw space opera game,too. Does the races have racial specific traits or are they just basically cosmetic ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12207-mahjemm01","name":"Mahjemm01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T06:42:48-07:00","id":950535,"title":"","content":"I've played, long ago, a AD&amp;D2e Dragonlance game were we were playing vampires form the Vampire: the Dark Ages. The DM used spells and other abilities from the various D&amp;D sourcebook to emulate the discipline. The thireteen clans were there, there was a proto-Camarilla, who served Bahamut, and the proto-Sabbat serving Tiamat. We've played three sessions and it was fun, but uterly broken. A few year latter, the DM revealed that the &quot;punch&quot; of the game was that the Antediluvian were, in fact, very old Dragons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2140-asimar","name":"Asimar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2140_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T09:09:02-07:00","id":951144,"title":"","content":"I have myself thought about mash-up idea about your, and my opinion is the best setting for a fantasy WoD would be mixing Ravenloft (by WotC), some ideas from Kult: lost divinity and Scarred Lands. Factions from vampire: dark age and mage: sorcerer's crusade are very interesting to be added to another fantasy worlds.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T05:47:47-07:00","id":968468,"title":"","content":"Our ST once told us he'd had an idea for a chronicle for quite a long time already he wanted to play and we did it. It was based on CWoD for rules as we all know that system quite well but the setting was different.<br /> It started with him telling us to create simple mortal characters living in the city we actually live in in RL. He gave us some restrictions on character creation (I think it was a dot less in attributes or some such thing, don't remember 100%).<br /> We figured out what each of our last memories were (our characters didn't know each other yet) and then we woke up in the basement of some house with some small clues, some basic supplies (batteries, flashlight, a bit of food, stuff like that) and with the door nailed shut wondering what had happened.<br /> When we left the house we found the city in pretty much an apocalyptic state with signs of corruption and dangerous supernatural creatures on the loose.<br /> He gave us a (RL) map of the city where several things were marked with not much of a clue as to what the markings meant.<br /> Later in the game we one by one discovered, that each of us was some kind of supernatural creature. Which one was randomly decided from a book about such things he had. I ended up finding out I was an initiate tempus mage (curiously without having any memory about being a member of such an order and having to find clues about this version of my past), another PC was a werewolf, another a Lamia. Good and evil were trying to convince us to join their respective sides (as a group or seperately). lots of hard choices to make and all. We werent able to leave the city either which added to the mystery.<br /> <br /> in the end it turned out to have been an artificially provoked dream that basically was our minds interpretation of a indoctrination programm while our bodies lay in a secret lab where military was trying to produce supernatural super-soldiers and the chronicle ended with us finding out about this, realising what was happening and breaking out of it. Joining &quot;Heaven&quot; would have meant the experiment was successful in producing an obedient soldier, joining &quot;Hell&quot; would have meant the experiment was successful in at least producing a supernatural murder-machine that can be thrown at an enemy. One of the PCs had actually joined the &quot;heaven&quot;-side for quite some time and my own character was very close to succumb to evil at one point but in the end we all managed to break out of the lab on our own will without succumbing to either.<br /> <br /> EDIT: now that I wrote all that I realise it doesnt really fit the question 100% as it technically wasn't set in an entirely different world. It was more a different plane of reality so to say. We went to a few other places (and times) as well when we discovered portals in a few places and other strange things happened (like my mage botching on a particularly difficult roll trying to achieve some time-magic effect)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11694,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","user":"Hexer","date":". 09-13-2016, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T07:06:32-07:00","id":969877,"title":"","content":"I haven't run it personally, but there's a very interesting looking conversion of the D&amp;D setting Planescape to M:tA rules: <a href=\"http://mimir.planewalker.com/sites/default/files/Planar-Mage.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Planar Mage</a>. (<a href=\"http://mimir.planewalker.com/sites/default/files/Planar-Mage-Races.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Planar Mage races</a>, <a href=\"http://mimir.planewalker.com/sites/default/files/Planar-Mage-DMG.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Planar Mage DMG</a>).<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Before enlightenment: chop wood, carry water. After enlightenment: Glorious Tree-Felling Prana and All-Encompassing Liquid-Carrying Methodology.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1223-dorchadas","name":"Dorchadas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1223_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T11:00:02-07:00","id":970044,"title":"","content":"Well, a few years ago i did a sword &amp; sorcery kind of game using a (completely made up) &quot;lost age&quot; sometime between the Impergium or just after it, where certain umbral spirits would grow fat and powerful upon ties with not just packs of garou but whole &quot;noble families&quot; of kinfolk heroes directing tribal nations though religious guidance or outright conquest, so, sort of a &quot;Werewolf meets Birtright with some touches of Conan' kind of setting and my players had loads of fun playing with it. In fact it was far from the only time i toyed with the &quot;lost mist-enshrouded era&quot; card while STing, as i once sketched a more crossover/gonzo &quot;A World Darkening&quot; chronicle, though that one didn't go all that far, unfortunately.<br /> <br /> Beside this once did a very funky crossover game extrapolating from the Mage's Digital Web and how it supposedly connected with other supernatural information webs (like the Malkavian's Madness Network among other stuff) to set up the Planescape-esque idea of Logos, the ocean where all datastreams flow, all knowledge can be found and <i>reality</i> separates from <i>fiction</i> by unclear arcane mechanisms not well-compreended (or perceived) even by those beings who believe themselves its, as plunging itself into the depths of what is and what is not can be a most complex (and perilous) matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T11:10:13-07:00","id":970051,"title":"","content":"Theirs the &quot;Wyld world&quot; Idea in book of the wyld, though its just earth with a radically different history.<br /> <br /> its hard to differentiate from exalted at times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T07:47:51-07:00","id":970688,"title":"","content":"While i have toyed with more openly fantastic or sci-fi settings of sorts, those came up while tinkering with nWoD (or CoD, as it's known now for the sake of clarity and independence).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T07:48:11-07:00","id":979015,"title":"","content":"Dark Ages Vampire in Westeros","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3701-augustus-dens","name":"Augustus Dens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3701_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T07:58:34-07:00","id":979019,"title":"","content":"Boltons as a Tzimisce Revenant House seeking to dethrone the Starks who are Silver Fang kinfolk. <br /> <br /> Roose Bolton wants to strike now cause the Starks haven't had a Garou member in generations. The Late Ned Stark didn't even teach his children about their history. Except that Roose doesn't realize that this generation might be different...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3701-augustus-dens","name":"Augustus Dens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3701_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T15:51:32-07:00","id":979298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mahjemm01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/950304-a-non-earth-world-of-darkness#post950304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has any one made a ST a chronicle using cWoD titles in a game that was not set in a Earth setting? Like for example, purely a example mind you, use WtA in a Faerun setting? Or Mage in a space opera setting? I have been toying with the idea and just curious if anyone else has done this</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but it's a very cool idea!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T19:13:22-07:00","id":981198,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, how could i forget, there was a crazy game i did for my kid cousins (back then, nowadays they have teen kids of their own, damn, do i feel old...) during a one month vacation in my aunt's beach house.<br /> <br /> Gory sword &amp; sorcery stuff using Masquerade for rules - a world of gods hungry for attention, worship and sacrifice, &quot;vitae&quot; (or stranger and even more dangerous stuff like balefire, ectoplasm, darkessence among others) might be sought and harvested from places of power holy, unholy or simply mysterious and any and all acts of ritual bloodletting, mutilation or sacrifice might be used to empower disciplines learned through study, seduction or toil on the feet of deity, demon or less identifiable beings. They really loved the crazy ultraviolence that sort of engendered in the setting while dealing with the challenge of not letting their humanity &amp; sanity plunge straight to the abyss along the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-03-2016, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}